{"id":"613e6ea21a4798c5b805d9e74535ced76642dd9e","axis":"silent","repo":"tinacms/tinacms","sha":"613e6ea21a4798c5b805d9e74535ced76642dd9e","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"packages/v4/@tinacms/tinacms/_docs/auth-plugins.md","lines":["@@ -66,6 +66,8 @@ A failure in `login()`, `logout()` or `getToken()` is an `AuthError`. It has a `"," |---|---|"," | `unauthenticated` | No session exists. |"," | `expired` | The session expired and did not refresh. |","+| `no-access` | The account has no access to this project. |","+| `popup-blocked` | The browser blocked the sign-in window. |"," | `network` | The sign-in service did not answer. |"," | `invalid-response` | The sign-in service sent a response that the plugin cannot read. |"," ","@@ -102,9 +104,10 @@ with no login.","   request reads `store.auth` and calls `getToken()` at the time it is sent."," - The local Data Layer (`tinaLocalDataLayerVitePlugin`) authorizes the","   content and media requests as the RPC handler does. It answers `401` when","-  there is no session, or when the auth plugin has no `getSession`. It","-  answers `403` when the roles do not grant the `requires` permission of the","-  content or media plugin. With no auth plugin, it checks nothing.","+  there is no session, or when the winning auth plugin has no `getSession`.","+  It answers `403` when the roles do not grant the `requires` permission of","+  the winning content or media plugin. With no auth plugin, or when the winning one has","+  no server segment, it checks nothing."," - The local Data Layer runs no `onInit`. A `getSession` must not depend on","   state that `onInit` sets."," - Roles and permissions are runtime data of the provider. They are not in","@@ -113,6 +116,54 @@ with no login.","   only. They hide controls that the editor cannot use. The server check is","   the security boundary."," ","+## TinaCloud","+","+`tinaCloud({ clientId })` is the reference auth plugin. It provides `auth`","+and `media` from one plugin.","+","+- `login()` signs in the way `https://identity.tinajs.io/v2/auth/config`","+  says, as v3 does:","+  - With `workosEnabled` off, it opens the TinaCloud sign-in popup at","+    `https://app.tina.io/signin`. The slice accepts the tokens only from a","+    message that the popup posts from the `https://app.tina.io` origin.","+  - With `workosEnabled` on, it redirects to","+    `https://identity.tinajs.io/v2/auth/tinacms` with a PKCE challenge. When","+    the browser returns with a `code` and the `state` this tab sent, the slice","+    exchanges the code at `/oauth/token` and restores the admin URL. The","+    verifier stays in `sessionStorage` for the round trip; the tokens do not.","+    A sign-in that fails on the way back sets `signed-out` with an `error`,","+    which the sign-in screen shows.","+- The slice reads the user from","+  `https://identity.tinajs.io/v2/apps/{clientId}/currentUser`, and their role","+  in the project from `https://identity.tinajs.io/v2/apps/{clientId}`. A","+  project `owner` or `admin`, or an org admin, gets the `admin` role, and any","+  other user gets `editor`.","+- An account with no access to the project fails with `no-access`.","+- An account that is not verified sets `forbidden`, and the slice keeps no","+  token for it. TinaCloud refuses a disabled account, so it fails with","+  `no-access`.","+- The tokens stay in a closure of the slice. A full reload signs the editor","+  out (ADR-023).","+- The media slice of `tinaCloud()` gets its token from the same closure. It","+  never reads the token of another auth plugin, so TinaCloud media needs","+  `tinaCloud()` to keep `auth`.","+- Before a media request, the closure refreshes the token through","+  `https://identity.tinajs.io/oauth/token` when it expires in less than two","+  minutes. A refused refresh sets `signed-out` and throws `expired`.","+","+The tokens only ever go to TinaCloud, as in v3. They are tied to the whole","+TinaCloud account, not to one project, so the slice's `getToken()` returns","+`undefined` and the site's own server never receives them. `tinaCloud()` has","+no server segment, so the local Data Layer checks nothing, as in v3, and the","+RPC handler refuses every operation that needs a session.","+","+```ts","+defineConfig({","+  plugins: [localContentPlugin(), tinaCloud({ clientId: '<client id>' })],","+  schema: { collections: [] },","+});","+```","+"," ## Swap a provider"," "," Core reads only the contract, so a change of provider is a change of plugin.","@@ -132,15 +183,15 @@ defineConfig({"," });"," ```"," ","-The overriding plugin mounts `store.auth`. For a plugin that provides more","-than one capability, the override replaces `auth` only, and the first plugin","-keeps its other capabilities.","+The overriding plugin mounts `store.auth` and answers `getSession`, so an","+override with no server segment leaves the RPC handler with no session. For a","+plugin that provides more than one capability, the override replaces `auth`","+only, and the first plugin keeps its other capabilities."," "," ## Not supported yet"," "," - Sign-out on a `401`. A request that carried a token and gets `401` fails,","   and the slice does not change its status.","-- An auth slice for `tinaCloud()`."," - `onLogin` and `onLogout` hooks in the config. A plugin does its own work","   inside its `login()` and `logout()`."," "],"additions":58,"deletions":7,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/v4/@tinacms/tinacms/_docs/media-plugins.md","lines":["@@ -119,8 +119,9 @@ through a symbolic link. It rejects a file name that holds a path separator."," "," ## `tinaCloud()`"," ","-`tinaCloud()` keeps media in TinaCloud. It provides `media`, with one slice in","-`slices.media`. A later release adds the `auth` capability to the same plugin.","+`tinaCloud()` keeps media in TinaCloud. It provides `media` and `auth`, with","+one slice in `slices.media` and one in `slices.auth`. Refer to","+[auth-plugins.md](./auth-plugins.md#tinacloud) for the sign-in flow."," "," ```ts"," import { defineConfig, localContentPlugin, tinaCloud } from '@tinacms/tinacms';","@@ -128,7 +129,7 @@ import { defineConfig, localContentPlugin, tinaCloud } from '@tinacms/tinacms';"," export default defineConfig({","   plugins: [","     localContentPlugin(),","-    tinaCloud({ clientId: '<client id>', getToken: () => readToken() }),","+    tinaCloud({ clientId: '<client id>' }),","   ],","   schema: { collections: [] },"," });","@@ -137,11 +138,9 @@ export default defineConfig({"," | Option | Role |"," |---|---|"," | `clientId` | The client ID of the TinaCloud project. |","-| `getToken` | Returns the TinaCloud access token of the editor, or `undefined`. It can return a promise. |"," ","-`getToken` is interim. When `tinaCloud()` provides `auth`, the plugin gets the","-token itself and the option goes. Until then, the app supplies the token. With","-no token, each operation fails with `unauthorized`.","+The media slice gets the token from the auth slice of the same plugin. Before","+the editor signs in, each operation fails with `unauthorized`."," "," The slice supplies `rename`, `features.search`, `features.extensionFilter` and"," a `features.maxSize` of 100 MB. `resolveUrl` gives a CDN URL, and a size adds","@@ -166,7 +165,6 @@ media branch, then keeps it for the session."," "," ### Not supported yet"," ","-- The `auth` capability. It replaces `getToken`."," - Media on an editorial workflow branch."," - Static media, built at build time."," - An assets API URL other than `https://assets.tinajs.io`."],"additions":6,"deletions":8,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/v4/@tinacms/tinacms/_docs/media.md","lines":["@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@ Note: the `media` capability is a single-provider capability; so we can only eve"," ```ts"," plugins: [","   localContentPlugin(),","-  isLocal ? localMediaPlugin() : tinaCloud({ clientId, getToken }),","+  isLocal ? localMediaPlugin() : tinaCloud({ clientId }),"," ]"," ```"," "],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/v4/@tinacms/tinacms/src/admin/auth-gate.test.tsx","lines":["@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@ import { QueryClient } from '@tanstack/react-query';"," import { render, screen } from '@testing-library/react';"," import userEvent from '@testing-library/user-event';"," import { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';","-import { type AuthSlice, toUserId } from '../core/auth/contract';","+import { AuthError, type AuthSlice, toUserId } from '../core/auth/contract';"," import { asResolvedConfig } from '../config';"," import { type PluginManifest, definePlugin } from '../core/plugin';"," import { testAuthPlugin } from '../test/test-auth-plugin';","@@ -76,6 +76,31 @@ describe('AuthGate', () => {","     expect(screen.queryByRole('list', { name: 'Collections' })).toBeNull();","   });"," ","+  it('shows why the last sign-in failed on the sign-in screen', async () => {","+    const failedAuthPlugin = definePlugin({","+      name: 'test:failed-auth',","+      provides: ['auth'],","+      client: async () => ({","+        default: {","+          slice: () =>","+            ({","+              status: 'signed-out',","+              user: null,","+              error: new AuthError('no-access'),","+              getToken: async () => undefined,","+              login: async () => {},","+              logout: async () => {},","+            }) satisfies AuthSlice,","+        },","+      }),","+    });","+    renderAdmin([failedAuthPlugin]);","+","+    expect(await screen.findByRole('alert')).toHaveTextContent(","+      'This account has no access to this project.'","+    );","+  });","+","   it(\"shows the plugin's own sign-in screen instead of the default\", async () => {","     const user = userEvent.setup();","     const formAuthPlugin = definePlugin({"],"additions":26,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/v4/@tinacms/tinacms/src/admin/auth-gate.tsx","lines":["@@ -1,21 +1,28 @@"," import { Button } from '@tinacms/ui/components/button';"," import { Skeleton } from '@tinacms/ui/components/skeleton';"," import type { ReactNode } from 'react';","-import type { AuthUser } from '../core/auth/contract';","+import type { AuthError, AuthUser } from '../core/auth/contract';"," import { useOptionalAuthSlice } from '../editor/hooks';"," import { useAuthAction } from './use-auth-action';"," ","-function SignInScreen({ login }: { login: () => Promise<void> }) {","+function SignInScreen({","+  login,","+  error,","+}: {","+  login: () => Promise<void>;","+  error?: AuthError;","+}) {","   const signIn = useAuthAction(login, 'Sign-in failed. Please try again.');","+  const message = signIn.pending ? null : (signIn.error ?? error?.message);","   return (","     <main className='flex min-h-svh flex-col items-center justify-center gap-4 p-4'>","       <h1 className='text-lg font-semibold'>Sign in to TinaCMS</h1>","       <Button onClick={signIn.run} disabled={signIn.pending}>","         Sign in","       </Button>","-      {signIn.error ? (","+      {message ? (","         <p role='alert' className='text-sm text-destructive'>","-          {signIn.error}","+          {message}","         </p>","       ) : null}","     </main>","@@ -67,5 +74,5 @@ export function AuthGate({ children }: { children: ReactNode }) {","     return <ForbiddenScreen user={auth.user} logout={auth.logout} />;","   }","   if (auth.LoginScreen) return <auth.LoginScreen />;","-  return <SignInScreen login={auth.login} />;","+  return <SignInScreen login={auth.login} error={auth.error} />;"," }"],"additions":12,"deletions":5,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/v4/@tinacms/tinacms/src/core/auth/contract.ts","lines":["@@ -40,6 +40,9 @@ export interface AuthTransportHooks {"," const AUTH_ERROR_MESSAGES = {","   unauthenticated: 'You are signed out. Sign in to continue.',","   expired: 'Your session has expired. Sign in again.',","+  'no-access': 'This account has no access to this project.',","+  'popup-blocked':","+    'The browser blocked the sign-in window. Allow popups for this site.',","   network: \"Can't reach the sign-in service. Check your connection.\",","   'invalid-response':","     'The sign-in service sent a response that Tina cannot read.',","@@ -62,11 +65,14 @@ export class AuthError extends Error {"," "," // ADR-023 §4/§5: the provider drives login and owns the token. The token stays in"," // memory, never in slice state or localStorage, and getToken refreshes it.","+// getToken is the token the site's own server receives; undefined sends none."," // ADR-008: `roles` gate the UI only. The server check is the security boundary."," export type AuthSlice = (","   | { status: 'signed-in'; user: AuthUser; roles: string[] }","   | { status: 'forbidden'; user: AuthUser }","-  | { status: 'loading' | 'signed-out'; user: null }","+  | { status: 'loading'; user: null }","+  // `error` is why a sign-in that did not run inside login() failed.","+  | { status: 'signed-out'; user: null; error?: AuthError }"," ) & {","   getToken(): Promise<string | undefined>;","   login(): Promise<void>;"],"additions":7,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/v4/@tinacms/tinacms/src/core/mount.ts","lines":["@@ -16,6 +16,21 @@ export const declaresCapabilityOverride = ("," ): boolean =>","   manifest.overrides.some((override) => override.capability === capability);"," ","+// The plugin that serves a singleton capability: its override, or else its one provider.","+export const capabilityProvider = (","+  plugins: PluginManifest[],","+  capability: Capability","+): PluginManifest | undefined => {","+  const providers = plugins.filter(({ provides }) =>","+    provides.includes(capability)","+  );","+  return (","+    providers.find((plugin) =>","+      declaresCapabilityOverride(plugin, capability)","+    ) ?? providers[0]","+  );","+};","+"," export const capabilityMountsFor = (","   manifest: PluginManifest"," ): CapabilityMount[] => {"],"additions":15,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/v4/@tinacms/tinacms/src/plugins/content/local/server/local-data-layer.vite.auth.test.ts","lines":["@@ -231,6 +231,48 @@ describe('local Data Layer with an auth plugin', () => {","     expect(res.statusCode).toBe(401);","   });"," ","+  it('checks sessions when a server auth plugin overrides a client-only one', async () => {","+    const clientOnlyAuth = definePlugin({","+      name: 'test:client-auth',","+      provides: ['auth'],","+    });","+    const override: PluginManifest = {","+      ...authPlugin,","+      name: 'test:override-auth',","+      overrides: [{ capability: 'auth' }],","+    };","+    const res = await sendNamed([clientOnlyAuth, override], 'content list', {","+      authorization: 'Bearer bad',","+    });","+    expect(res.statusCode).toBe(401);","+  });","+","+  it('checks nothing when a client-only auth plugin overrides a server one', async () => {","+    const clientOnlyOverride = definePlugin({","+      name: 'test:client-auth',","+      provides: ['auth'],","+      overrides: [{ capability: 'auth' }],","+    });","+    const res = await sendNamed(","+      [authPlugin, clientOnlyOverride],","+      'content list'","+    );","+    expect(res.statusCode).toBe(200);","+  });","+","+  it('checks the permission the winning media plugin requires', async () => {","+    const override: PluginManifest = {","+      ...localMediaPlugin(),","+      name: 'test:media',","+      overrides: [{ capability: 'media' }],","+      requires: { permission: 'media:admin' },","+    };","+    const res = await sendNamed([authPlugin, override], 'media list', {","+      authorization: 'Bearer good',","+    });","+    expect(res.statusCode).toBe(403);","+  });","+","   it('resolves use(capability) inside getSession', async () => {","     const composingAuth = authPluginWith({","       ping: async () => true,"],"additions":42,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/v4/@tinacms/tinacms/src/plugins/content/local/server/local-data-layer.vite.ts","lines":["@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@ import { runCodegen } from '../../../../cli/commands/codegen';"," import { type ResolvedConfig, resolveBuild } from '../../../../config';"," import { DEFAULT_CONTENT_URL } from '../../../../core/content/contract';"," import { invariant } from '../../../../core/invariant';","+import { capabilityProvider } from '../../../../core/mount';"," import { DEFAULT_MEDIA_URL, MediaError } from '../../../../core/media/contract';"," import {","   MAX_MEDIA_UPLOAD_BYTES,","@@ -140,18 +141,16 @@ type SessionGate = ("," ) => Promise<boolean>;"," "," // ADR-023 §4: with an auth plugin, the Data Layer authorizes a request as","-// rpc/handler.ts does. With no auth plugin, it composes nothing and checks nothing.","+// rpc/handler.ts does. When no auth plugin, or the winning one has no server","+// segment, it composes nothing and checks nothing."," const createSessionGate = (","   plugins: PluginManifest[],","   capability: 'content' | 'media'"," ): SessionGate | null => {","-  if (!plugins.some(({ provides }) => provides.includes(AUTH_CAPABILITY))) {","-    return null;","-  }","+  if (!capabilityProvider(plugins, AUTH_CAPABILITY)?.server) return null;","   const authorize = createRequestAuthorizer(plugins);","-  const permission = plugins.find(({ provides }) =>","-    provides.includes(capability)","-  )?.requires?.permission;","+  const permission = capabilityProvider(plugins, capability)?.requires","+    ?.permission;","   return async (req, res) => {","     try {","       const refusal = await authorize(sessionRequestOf(req), [permission]);"],"additions":6,"deletions":7,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/v4/@tinacms/tinacms/src/plugins/tinacloud/auth/popup.ts","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,76 @@","+import type { z } from 'zod';","+import { AuthError } from '../../../core/auth/contract';","+","+const POPUP_POLL_MS = 500;","+","+export const openCenteredPopup = (","+  url: URL,","+  width: number,","+  height: number","+): Window => {","+  const left = window.screenX + (window.outerWidth - width) / 2;","+  const top = window.screenY + (window.outerHeight - height) / 2;","+  const popup = window.open(","+    url,","+    '_blank',","+    `popup,width=${width},height=${height},left=${left},top=${top}`","+  );","+  if (!popup) {","+    throw new AuthError('popup-blocked', 'window.open returned null.');","+  }","+  return popup;","+};","+","+export const waitForPopupMessage = <Message>(","+  popup: Window,","+  {","+    origin,","+    isCandidate,","+    schema,","+  }: {","+    origin: string;","+    isCandidate: (data: unknown) => boolean;","+    schema: z.ZodType<Message>;","+  }","+): Promise<Message> =>","+  new Promise((resolve, reject) => {","+    const controller = new AbortController();","+    const settle = (finish: () => void) => {","+      controller.abort();","+      finish();","+    };","+    window.addEventListener(","+      'message',","+      (event) => {","+        if (event.origin !== origin || event.source !== popup) return;","+        if (!isCandidate(event.data)) return;","+        popup.close();","+        const parsed = schema.safeParse(event.data);","+        if (parsed.success) {","+          settle(() => resolve(parsed.data));","+        } else {","+          settle(() =>","+            reject(","+              new AuthError(","+                'invalid-response',","+                'The sign-in popup sent a message in an unknown format.'","+              )","+            )","+          );","+        }","+      },","+      { signal: controller.signal }","+    );","+    const poll = setInterval(() => {","+      if (!popup.closed) return;","+      settle(() =>","+        reject(","+          new AuthError(","+            'unauthenticated',","+            'The sign-in popup closed before sign-in finished.'","+          )","+        )","+      );","+    }, POPUP_POLL_MS);","+    controller.signal.addEventListener('abort', () => clearInterval(poll));","+  });"],"additions":76,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/v4/@tinacms/tinacms/src/plugins/tinacloud/auth/redirect.ts","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,122 @@","+import { z } from 'zod';","+import { AuthError } from '../../../core/auth/contract';","+import { TINACLOUD_IDENTITY_URL } from '../client';","+","+// The verifier only has to outlive the round trip to TinaCloud, so it stays in","+// this tab's sessionStorage. No token is ever stored.","+const PKCE_STORAGE_KEY = 'tinacms-tinacloud-pkce';","+","+const pendingSignInSchema = z.object({","+  clientId: z.string(),","+  verifier: z.string(),","+  state: z.string(),","+  search: z.string(),","+  hash: z.string(),","+});","+","+export interface RedirectResult {","+  code: string;","+  verifier: string;","+  redirectUri: string;","+}","+","+/**","+ * A redirect sign-in this tab started. `outcome` is set when the page has just","+ * come back from TinaCloud, and holds the code to exchange or why it failed.","+ */","+export interface PendingRedirect {","+  state: string;","+  outcome?: RedirectResult | AuthError;","+}","+","+const base64Url = (bytes: Uint8Array) =>","+  btoa(String.fromCharCode(...bytes))","+    .replace(/\\+/g, '-')","+    .replace(/\\//g, '_')","+    .replace(/=+$/, '');","+","+const randomToken = (byteLength: number) =>","+  base64Url(crypto.getRandomValues(new Uint8Array(byteLength)));","+","+const challengeOf = async (verifier: string) =>","+  base64Url(","+    new Uint8Array(","+      await crypto.subtle.digest('SHA-256', new TextEncoder().encode(verifier))","+    )","+  );","+","+const redirectUri = () => window.location.origin + window.location.pathname;","+","+const readPendingSignIn = () => {","+  try {","+    const parsed = pendingSignInSchema.safeParse(","+      JSON.parse(sessionStorage.getItem(PKCE_STORAGE_KEY) ?? 'null')","+    );","+    return parsed.success ? parsed.data : undefined;","+  } catch {","+    return undefined;","+  }","+};","+","+export const clearPendingRedirect = () => {","+  sessionStorage.removeItem(PKCE_STORAGE_KEY);","+};","+","+/** Sends the browser to TinaCloud's WorkOS sign-in, which returns with `?code&state`. */","+export const startRedirectSignIn = async (clientId: string) => {","+  const verifier = randomToken(64);","+  const state = randomToken(32);","+  const { search, hash } = window.location;","+  sessionStorage.setItem(","+    PKCE_STORAGE_KEY,","+    JSON.stringify({ clientId, verifier, state, search, hash })","+  );","+  const params = new URLSearchParams({","+    response_type: 'code',","+    client_id: clientId,","+    redirect_uri: redirectUri(),","+    code_challenge: await challengeOf(verifier),","+    code_challenge_method: 'S256',","+    state,","+  });","+  window.location.assign(`${TINACLOUD_IDENTITY_URL}/v2/auth/tinacms?${params}`);","+};","+","+/** Reads the redirect sign-in this tab started, and restores the URL it left from. */","+export const readPendingRedirect = (","+  clientId: string","+): PendingRedirect | undefined => {","+  const pending = readPendingSignIn();","+  if (!pending || pending.clientId !== clientId) return undefined;","+  const params = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search);","+  const code = params.get('code');","+  const error = params.get('error');","+  if (!code && !error) return { state: pending.state };","+  window.history.replaceState(","+    null,","+    '',","+    redirectUri() + pending.search + pending.hash","+  );","+  if (error) {","+    return {","+      state: pending.state,","+      outcome: new AuthError(","+        'unauthenticated',","+        `TinaCloud returned the sign-in with ${error}.`","+      ),","+    };","+  }","+  if (!code || params.get('state') !== pending.state) {","+    return {","+      state: pending.state,","+      outcome: new AuthError(","+        'unauthenticated',","+        'The sign-in returned with a state that this tab did not send.'","+      ),","+    };","+  }","+  return {","+    state: pending.state,","+    outcome: { code, verifier: pending.verifier, redirectUri: redirectUri() },","+  };","+};"],"additions":122,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/v4/@tinacms/tinacms/src/plugins/tinacloud/auth/tinacloud-auth-types.ts","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,68 @@","+import { z } from 'zod';","+import { type AuthUser, toUserId } from '../../../core/auth/contract';","+import { TINACLOUD_IDENTITY_URL } from '../client';","+","+export const TINACLOUD_LOGIN_EVENT = 'tinaCloudLogin';","+","+export const loginMessageSchema = z.object({","+  source: z.literal(TINACLOUD_LOGIN_EVENT),","+  access_token: z.string().min(1),","+  id_token: z.string().min(1).optional(),","+  refresh_token: z.string().min(1),","+});","+","+export type TinaCloudLoginMessage = z.infer<typeof loginMessageSchema>;","+","+export const refreshResponseSchema = z.object({","+  access_token: z.string().min(1),","+  id_token: z.string().min(1).optional(),","+  refresh_token: z.string().min(1).optional(),","+});","+","+export const codeResponseSchema = refreshResponseSchema.required({","+  refresh_token: true,","+});","+","+export const authConfigSchema = z.object({ workosEnabled: z.boolean() });","+","+export const jwtPayloadSchema = z.object({ exp: z.number() });","+","+// TinaCloud sends a missing name or email as \"\".","+const optionalText = z","+  .string()","+  .optional()","+  .transform((text) => text || undefined);","+","+export const currentUserSchema = z","+  .object({","+    id: optionalText,","+    email: optionalText,","+    fullName: optionalText,","+    verified: z.boolean().optional(),","+  })","+  .transform(({ id, email, fullName, verified }, context) => {","+    const userId = id ?? email;","+    if (!userId) {","+      context.addIssue({","+        code: z.ZodIssueCode.custom,","+        message: 'The user has no id and no email.',","+      });","+      return z.NEVER;","+    }","+    const user: AuthUser = { id: toUserId(userId), name: fullName, email };","+    return { user, active: verified === true };","+  });","+","+// As TinaCloud's CanAdminApp: a project owner or admin, or an org admin or","+// superuser, whose role TinaCloud sends as \"\" because they have no project row.","+export const projectRolesSchema = z","+  .object({ role: z.string().optional() })","+  .transform(({ role = '' }) => [","+    ['', 'admin', 'owner'].includes(role.toLowerCase()) ? 'admin' : 'editor',","+  ]);","+","+export const projectUrl = (clientId: string) =>","+  `${TINACLOUD_IDENTITY_URL}/v2/apps/${encodeURIComponent(clientId)}`;","+","+export const currentUserUrl = (clientId: string) =>","+  `${projectUrl(clientId)}/currentUser`;"],"additions":68,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/v4/@tinacms/tinacms/src/plugins/tinacloud/auth/tinacloud-auth.client.test.ts","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,563 @@","+import { afterEach, beforeEach, describe, expect, it, vi } from 'vitest';","+import { AuthError } from '../../../core/auth/contract';","+import type { SliceState } from '../../../core/plugin';","+import {","+  jwtExpiringIn,","+  loginTokens,","+  postMessageFrom,","+  stubLoginPopup,","+  tinaCloudIdentity,","+  tinaCloudUser,","+} from '../../../test/tinacloud-login';","+import { TINACLOUD_IDENTITY_URL } from '../client';","+import { createTinaCloudAuth } from './tinacloud-auth.client';","+","+const CURRENT_USER_URL = `${TINACLOUD_IDENTITY_URL}/v2/apps/abc/currentUser`;","+","+const PROJECT_URL = `${TINACLOUD_IDENTITY_URL}/v2/apps/abc`;","+","+const AUTH_CONFIG_URL = `${TINACLOUD_IDENTITY_URL}/v2/auth/config`;","+","+const TOKEN_URL = `${TINACLOUD_IDENTITY_URL}/oauth/token`;","+","+const json = (body: unknown, status = 200) =>","+  new Response(JSON.stringify(body), { status });","+","+const stubFetch = (","+  respond: (url: string, init?: RequestInit) => Response | Promise<Response>","+) => {","+  const fetchMock = vi.fn(async (url: string, init?: RequestInit) =>","+    respond(url, init)","+  );","+  vi.stubGlobal('fetch', fetchMock);","+  return fetchMock;","+};","+","+const boot = () => {","+  const auth = createTinaCloudAuth({ clientId: 'abc' });","+  const state: SliceState = {};","+  const slice = auth.slice((partial) => {","+    Object.assign(","+      state,","+      typeof partial === 'function' ? partial(state) : partial","+    );","+  });","+  Object.assign(state, slice);","+  return { slice, state, tinaCloudToken: auth.tinaCloudToken };","+};","+","+const signIn = async (tokens = loginTokens()) => {","+  const { complete } = stubLoginPopup();","+  const booted = boot();","+  const login = booted.slice.login();","+  complete(tokens);","+  await login;","+  return booted;","+};","+","+beforeEach(() => {","+  stubFetch((url) => tinaCloudIdentity(url));","+});","+","+afterEach(() => {","+  sessionStorage.clear();","+  window.history.replaceState(null, '', '/');","+  vi.restoreAllMocks();","+  vi.unstubAllGlobals();","+  vi.useRealTimers();","+});","+","+describe('TinaCloud auth slice', () => {","+  it('starts signed out with no token', async () => {","+    const { state, tinaCloudToken } = boot();","+    expect(state).toMatchObject({ status: 'signed-out', user: null });","+    expect(await tinaCloudToken()).toBeUndefined();","+  });","+","+  it('signs in through the TinaCloud popup and keeps the token in memory', async () => {","+    const fetchMock = stubFetch((url) => tinaCloudIdentity(url));","+    const { popup, open, complete } = stubLoginPopup();","+    const { slice, state, tinaCloudToken } = boot();","+","+    const login = slice.login();","+    complete();","+    await login;","+","+    const [url] = open.mock.calls[0];","+    expect(String(url)).toBe(","+      `https://app.tina.io/signin?clientId=abc&origin=${encodeURIComponent(window.location.origin)}`","+    );","+    expect(popup.close).toHaveBeenCalled();","+    expect(fetchMock.mock.calls.map(([url]) => url)).toEqual([","+      AUTH_CONFIG_URL,","+      CURRENT_USER_URL,","+      PROJECT_URL,","+    ]);","+    expect(","+      new Headers(fetchMock.mock.calls[1][1]?.headers).get('Authorization')","+    ).toBe('Bearer id-token');","+    expect(state).toMatchObject({","+      status: 'signed-in',","+      user: { id: 'ada', name: 'Ada Lovelace', email: 'ada@example.com' },","+      roles: ['admin'],","+    });","+    expect(JSON.stringify(state)).not.toContain('id-token');","+    expect(localStorage.length).toBe(0);","+    expect(await tinaCloudToken()).toBe('id-token');","+  });","+","+  it('ignores messages from another origin or another window', async () => {","+    const fetchMock = stubFetch((url) => tinaCloudIdentity(url));","+    const { popup, opened, complete } = stubLoginPopup();","+    const { slice, state } = boot();","+","+    const login = slice.login();","+    await opened();","+    postMessageFrom(popup, loginTokens(), 'https://evil.example');","+    postMessageFrom(window, loginTokens());","+    postMessageFrom(popup, { ...loginTokens(), source: 'other' });","+    expect(popup.close).not.toHaveBeenCalled();","+    expect(fetchMock).toHaveBeenCalledOnce();","+","+    complete();","+    await login;","+    expect(state.status).toBe('signed-in');","+  });","+","+  it('rejects with unauthenticated when the editor closes the popup', async () => {","+    vi.useFakeTimers();","+    const { popup, opened } = stubLoginPopup();","+    const { slice, state } = boot();","+","+    const login = slice.login();","+    await opened();","+    const assertion = expect(login).rejects.toMatchObject({","+      code: 'unauthenticated',","+      detail: expect.stringContaining('closed'),","+    });","+    popup.closed = true;","+    await vi.advanceTimersByTimeAsync(500);","+    await assertion;"],"additions":140,"deletions":0,"truncated":false}],"additions":579,"deletions":30,"truncated":true,"file_count":13},"error":null,"fetched_at":"2026-10-13T15:27:45.487132+00:00"}